// Q: What if We Don't Write a Constructor?

// ANS: Suppose

// class Student
// {
// public:

//     int age;
// };

// No constructor.

// Now

// Student s1;

// Will it compile?

// Yes.

// Because the compiler creates one for you.

// This is called the default constructor generated by the compiler.

// It has no parameters.

// Conceptually:

// Student()
// {


// }

// The compiler only generates this if you do not write any constructor yourself.